	* Laravel : This code implements an SLA (Service Level Agreement) calculation system for support tickets within the application. It includes logic to compute key SLA times such as:

	First Response Time: The time it takes to respond to a support ticket after it is opened.
	Resolve Time: The total time to resolve a support ticket.
	Alert Times: Notification times before the first response and before resolution, based on configured SLA targets.

	The SlaService class interacts with several models (e.g., Supportticket, IncidentType, SlaTarget, SlaSetting) to gather necessary data and performs the following tasks:

	Fetches ticket details and SLA targets based on ticket priority, incident type, and user level.
	Handles business hours and ensures that the calculated SLA times account for off days and holidays.
	Provides methods to calculate SLA times considering business start/end times, holidays, off days, and dynamic priority-based SLA configurations.
	Logs detailed information for debugging and tracking SLA calculations.

	This service ensures that the SLA metrics are correctly calculated and aligned with business rules defined in the application settings. 

